    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30945" root="عود" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَوَادٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُوَادَةٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُدْ فَإِنَّ لَكَ عِنْدَنَا عَوَادًا حَسَنًا</span>,
(S, O, K,) as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُوَادًا</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِوَادًا</span>, (O, K,) these
two only, not the first, mentioned by Fr, (O,)
means [<i>Return thou, and thou shalt have with us</i>]
<i>what thou wilt like:</i> (S, O, K:) or <i>kind treatment.</i> (TA.)

